  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1150 AM CDT Fri Aug 21 2026\n\nTroughing will remain in place this weekend with northwesterly \nflow persisting across our region. This will favor slightly \nbelow-normal temperatures with cooler overnight conditions into \nMonday. The trough will slowly migrate east by Tuesday which will \nhelp bring temperatures up a couple degrees. This will also open \nthe door for an axis of higher PWs/instability to push into the \narea from the west. At least a couple of passing shortwave \nperturbations are progged to move through the northwesterly flow \naloft which should foster isolated to scattered rain/storms \nTuesday through Thursday. Forecast temperatures are essential \nright at seasonal norms most days next week.",
